WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.570
When I first started
bringing my kids in the woods,

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.305
I wasn't sure how
they take to it.

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:07.540
And it seems like
it's in their blood.

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:08.808
Makes me feel real proud.

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:11.978
[music playing]

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.351
Go check out the bath house.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:21.454
We got some work
to do ahead of us.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:22.889
Part of having
these hot springs is

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:24.524
taking care of the hot springs.

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:27.427
There's a cold stream that
flows next to the bath house.

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:29.229
What we're going to
do is start working

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:30.930
to get this whole
place cleaned out,

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:32.799
take all the mud out,
and hopefully come

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.701
away with a beautiful bathtub.

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:40.306
What we want to do is take
these rocks out here and kind

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:43.777
of divert the stream going in.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.945
We're just getting all
this water to flow through.

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:48.047
And then it'll take
all the mud with it?

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:48.748
Yeah.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:49.816
Well, not all this mud.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:51.584
But inside we could
stir it up, and get

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:54.554
that mud and stuff that's in
there on the pallet washed out.

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:55.455
OK.

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:57.590
Let's go inside.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:00.026
Put on some rubber boots.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:02.996
I want to teach Skyler a little
bit of community service.

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:04.564
A lot of us use
these hot springs.

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:05.899
A lot of us use this bath house.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.634
And fixing this bath
house is teaching

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.803
him how to be a better person.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:14.707
When it comes to an area,
he leaves it a better place.

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:15.642
Let's see that bucket.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:16.743
I could fill it up with mud.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.011
You can just carry it.

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:21.414
Out last time this is done
is probably a year or so.

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.650
The mud has really built up.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.885
[music playing]

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.887
OK.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:30.356
Well, let's keep taking
loads of mud out of here.

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:33.960
What we want is a sand
bottom not a mud bottom.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.562
Get all this mud up.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:40.533
Very dark, black mud comes
from deep within the Earth.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.369
And it basically just settles
inside of that bathtub.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:46.439
What I'm trying to do is take
a good 6 to 8 inches of mud

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.908
off the bottom of this
bathtub, so it gets

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:51.611
to clean, clear water inside.

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.880
Life's too short
for a muddy bath.

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:56.316
[music playing]

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.284
It's getting down to
the sand, though, Sky.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.185
You are?

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.119
Yeah.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.421
We are.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:02.989
You're doing a lot of work.

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:04.390
Skyler is working his butt off.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:07.927
He's taking these pans of
mud and dumping them outside.

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:10.497
And they're ready to
be filled up again.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:13.766
Working together like this,
we get a lot of work done.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:14.701
OK.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:15.602
Oh!

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:16.903
That was heavy.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.441
OK, Sky.

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:22.876
Looks like we're
about done in here.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:23.877
We got it down to sand.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.112
All the mud's out.

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:28.715
Good job on carrying
all that dirt out.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.416
With Skyler's help,
we were able to clean

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.385
that entryway out
completely of mud,

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:34.120
and it's looking beautiful now.

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.455
It looks good.

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:37.590
You want to close that stream
off out there real quick?

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:37.957
Yeah.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:38.658
OK.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:39.425
I'm going to dry off.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.693
Shut that cold water down.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.395
We're done with it.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.963
People at home in
the city, they're

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.533
using the cold knob and
the hot knob on the faucet

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.067
to get that perfect temperature.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:49.802
That's what me and
Skyler are doing today,

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:52.138
but we're using a creek
and the hot springs

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:54.874
to work out a perfect
temperature in this bath house.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:57.110
We really blocked
this off right here.

00:02:57.176 --> 00:03:00.013
[music playing]

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:02.382
It should be good.

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:06.286
My job in the hot
tub is complete.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:09.389
[music playing]

